Subject: [PATCH] keyguard: a pending hide must not undo a show

With the screen lock set to None and a SIM that asks for its PIN, the PIN
screen came up under the boot animation and was gone 36 ms later. The SIM
stayed locked and nothing on screen said so.

When the system becomes ready, doKeyguardLocked() finds the lock screen
switched off and queues a HIDE. The SIM state arrives next, PIN required,
and doKeyguardLocked() runs again: this time it calls showLocked(), which
sends SHOW to the front of the queue. At boot the main thread is seconds
behind, the HIDE is still waiting, and it is handled after the SHOW that was
requested later. With any other screen lock the first call queues nothing,
which is why the PIN was asked there.

A show request cancels the hides queued before it.
---
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -1507,6 +1507,10 @@
         // ensure we stay awake until we are finished displaying the keyguard
         mShowKeyguardWakeLock.acquire();
         Message msg = mHandler.obtainMessage(SHOW, options);
+        // SHOW goes to the front of the queue, so a HIDE requested before it and not handled
+        // yet would run after it and take the keyguard away again. Whoever asks to show now
+        // has seen everything that request was based on: drop it.
+        mHandler.removeMessages(HIDE);
         // Treat these messages with priority - This call can originate from #doKeyguardTimeout,
         // meaning the device should lock as soon as possible and not wait for other messages on
         // the thread to process first.
